 "root_cause": "Model skill writes owned only individual public save/get/state/rollback operations. Patch and state transitions could lose the handoff between these stages on waiter cancellation, while archive/restore initial head queries bypassed service admission. The final model receipt was outside the owned operation.",
 "changes": [
  "Own each of six model write tools from first preparation/head lookup through final guarded commit and receipt, under the existing eight admissions/two slots",
  "Extract unchanged public mutation operation bodies into already-admitted internal save/state/rollback helpers; public entry points keep independent admission",
  "Use internal verified get/save/state/rollback within model writes to avoid nested slot acquisition or re-admission during draining",
  "Keep final approved_dispatch callback, revision/CAS and revocation checks, object publication/reference handling, disabled-review state and exact receipt",
  "Preserve caller/close cancellation shielding without replay; remove one now-unnecessary str cast after scope extraction"
 ],
